tablecloth-wearing Asian...


00:13:01.027 --> 00:13:03.257
- Indian.
- Who makes no sense at all, ever.


00:13:03.429 --> 00:13:05.192
Why don't you have another drink, Mom.


00:13:06.733 --> 00:13:08.928
Katie, napkin me.


00:13:09.102 --> 00:13:11.593
I have got to impress Guy Morgan...


00:13:12.005 --> 00:13:15.236
...so I can stop pretending to care
about this insufferable school...


00:13:15.408 --> 00:13:19.174
...and we can all move to Hollywood where
no one pretends to care about anything.


00:13:19.345 --> 00:13:22.974
Mom, I think that you're forgetting
about the most important thing. Me.


00:13:23.916 --> 00:13:26.316
Guy will give me a deal
as soon as he hears me sing.


00:13:26.486 --> 00:13:29.080
- I doubt that.
- No, I've been practicing really hard.


00:13:29.255 --> 00:13:32.122
My voice teacher says
I've transcended to a whole new level.


00:13:32.292 --> 00:13:33.316
Yeah, I doubt it.


00:13:33.493 --> 00:13:36.053
When my first single drops,
I'll buy you that mansion...


00:13:36.229 --> 00:13:38.163
...in the Hollywood Hills...


00:13:38.331 --> 00:13:41.357
...and you can finally afford
to have your legs lengthened.


00:13:41.534 --> 00:13:43.559
- Oh, ba...
- Ms. Gail.


00:13:43.736 --> 00:13:45.704
- Miss Bev has clarity.
Katie.


00:13:45.872 --> 00:13:46.896
- You see...
- Look.


00:13:47.073 --> 00:13:50.941
- The lowly peasant tills the soil
for 40 years without any rain.


00:13:51.110 --> 00:13:54.511
But the unemployed salesman
who has recently discovered hydroponics...


00:13:54.681 --> 00:13:57.775
...all of a sudden gets disgusted by the...
- And see? No sense.


00:13:57.950 --> 00:14:00.248
- That didn't make any sense.
- Let me finish. You...


00:14:00.420 --> 00:14:02.354
Oh, I doubt it. You have me pray all day.


00:14:02.522 --> 00:14:04.752
- I don't feel nothing.
- You don't have a soul.


00:14:04.924 --> 00:14:08.121
No, you don't have soul.
- I have a many souls. I'll give you one.


00:14:08.294 --> 00:14:12.560
- Where's your third eye? Turn that thing on.
- I have a fourth eye too. You wanna see it?


00:14:12.732 --> 00:14:14.700
- What?
- Shh.


00:14:15.201 --> 00:14:18.728
I wanna be 6'4". Wow me, Bev.


00:14:21.274 --> 00:14:26.712
<i>Do-re-mi-fa-so-la-ti-do</i>


00:14:26.879 --> 00:14:29.439
Just stop. Stop the wowing, okay?


00:14:29.615 --> 00:14:31.708
What's wrong?
- Somehow you've gotten worse.


00:14:31.884 --> 00:14:33.613
I don't know how that was possible...


00:14:33.786 --> 00:14:36.414
...but there isn't enough Auto-Tune
that's gonna fix you.


00:14:36.589 --> 00:14:39.922
- Well, Katie's bad playing threw me off.
- I don't think it was that.


00:14:40.093 --> 00:14:41.720
Again.


00:14:41.894 --> 00:14:43.452
Really? Okay.


00:14:43.629 --> 00:14:49.261
<i>Do-re-mi-fa-so-la-ti-do</i>


00:14:49.435 --> 00:14:50.561
Ouch.


00:14:50.737 --> 00:14:53.797
I could belch the song better.


00:14:55.408 --> 00:14:57.569
Have you been drinking
the floor wax again?


00:14:57.744 --> 00:14:59.211
Anything to forget I live here.


00:14:59.379 --> 00:15:02.280
Ugh. My head is buzzing
like a skeeter on a septic tank.


00:15:02.448 --> 00:15:06.350
- Ravi, meditate me.
Good luck, buddy.


00:15:06.719 --> 00:15:10.382
Well, it doesn't matter,
because I have my own plan.


00:15:14.594 --> 00:15:16.960
Does it make me a bad person
that I kind of enjoyed that?


00:15:17.130 --> 00:15:18.859
No.


00:15:19.031 --> 00:15:21.329
Hmm. Nice work.


00:15:33.513 --> 00:15:36.812
- Guess who's on his way over.
- Not now, Victor, I'm busy.


00:15:36.983 --> 00:15:39.451
Guess or prepare to get creamed.


00:15:49.929 --> 00:15:53.023
Victor! Victor! Victor, stop!


00:15:57.904 --> 00:15:59.633
<i>I've got rings on my fingers</i>


00:15:59.806 --> 00:16:00.898
<i>And glitter in my hair</i>


00:16:01.073 --> 00:16:05.169
<i>I've got a one-way ticket
And I just got here</i>


00:16:05.344 --> 00:16:06.675
<i>I'm gonna run...</i>


00:16:06.846 --> 00:16:09.610
- Ha-ha-ha.
- Victor, what are you doing?


00:16:10.049 --> 00:16:11.346
Victor!


00:16:11.517 --> 00:16:14.748
Victor, where did you put my clothes?


00:16:14.921 --> 00:16:17.082
- Surprise!
- What? No.


00:16:20.593 --> 00:16:22.220
I'm gonna kill you. Victor!


00:16:32.138 --> 00:16:33.298
Oh, hi, Katie.


00:16:33.473 --> 00:16:34.872
You are evil. Let me in.


00:16:35.041 --> 00:16:38.477
I control every lock on this property.


00:16:38.644 --> 00:16:40.305
Crap.


00:16:43.716 --> 00:16:45.411
This is insane.


00:16:45.585 --> 00:16:49.646
Yeah, try the shed, it's unlocked, idiot.


00:16:59.432 --> 00:17:01.525
You gotta be kidding me.


00:17:03.269 --> 00:17:04.896
Crap.


00:17:08.207 --> 00:17:11.802
How did such an untalented daughter
spring from my loins?


00:17:11.978 --> 00:17:15.778
Focus, Ms. Gail. We are making
an offering to your personal deity.


00:17:15.948 --> 00:17:18.075
Tell him to give me fame and fortune.


00:17:18.251 --> 00:17:19.946
Not exactly how it works.


00:17:20.119 --> 00:17:22.679
<i>Now, breathe through your Mula Bandha.</i>


00:17:22.855 --> 00:17:25.915
Oh, honey, if I could do that,
I'd get a million hits on YouTube.


00:17:26.092 --> 00:17:28.322
How much longer is this gonna take?
Ugh.


00:17:28.494 --> 00:17:30.621
The prayer or the fame and fortune?


00:17:32.965 --> 00:17:34.432
Ha, ha. See you later.


00:17:40.606 --> 00:17:42.471
Victor.


00:17:46.312 --> 00:17:47.745
Katie?


00:17:48.948 --> 00:17:51.178
- Luke.
- Katie.


00:17:51.384 --> 00:17:54.649
- Are you wearing a doormat?
- Yes.


00:17:54.820 --> 00:17:57.584
- Welcome.
- Why, thank you.


00:17:58.624 --> 00:18:00.455
The truth. Um...


00:18:01.761 --> 00:18:05.094
My stepbrother locked me
outside of the house.


00:18:05.264 --> 00:18:06.595
Naked.


00:18:07.633 --> 00:18:09.931
Oh, sorry. You should...
You should take my jacket.


00:18:10.102 --> 00:18:11.626
Oh.
- Oh, no, no.


00:18:14.073 --> 00:18:15.165
There.


00:18:15.341 --> 00:18:18.538
- Thanks. Now the pants.
- Hmm?


00:18:23.149 --> 00:18:24.776
I'm kidding.


00:18:25.318 --> 00:18:27.149
- You got me.
- Ha, ha.


00:18:27.486 --> 00:18:28.510
No, no.


00:18:28.688 --> 00:18:32.089
One more parent-teacher conference,
I swear I'm gonna lose it.


00:18:32.258 --> 00:18:34.453
Look at me. I'm an educator.


00:18:35.061 --> 00:18:39.725
I have no real skills. And I will die
before I go back to my daddy's farm.


00:18:40.232 --> 00:18:44.032
You tell my personal deity
to help me achieve Guy Morgan. Do it.


00:18:44.203 --> 00:18:46.797
I'll put another banana on the altar.


00:18:50.676 --> 00:18:52.337
What is that?


00:18:52.912 --> 00:18:55.176
Do you hear angels singing?


00:18:55.348 --> 00:18:57.316
Perhaps the gods
have answered your prayer.


00:18:58.517 --> 00:19:00.246
Hey. What...?


00:19:13.099 --> 00:19:15.590
<i>- This is Gail Van Ravensway.
Hello.</i>


00:19:15.768 --> 00:19:17.395
Guy Morgan here. How are you?


00:19:17.570 --> 00:19:19.697
Oh, well, hello, Guy.


00:19:19.872 --> 00:19:22.136
What a surprise
to see you calling this number.


00:19:22.308 --> 00:19:23.332
Do you hear this?


00:19:23.509 --> 00:19:25.170
<i>I can justify</i>


00:19:25.344 --> 00:19:27.039
That's the demo your girl, Katie...


00:19:27.213 --> 00:19:29.545
<i>... slipped into my briefcase.</i>


00:19:29.715 --> 00:19:31.910
And it sounds like money, dear.


00:19:32.084 --> 00:19:33.949
She gave you a CD?


00:19:34.120 --> 00:19:37.487
Oh, well. Well, ain't that the berries.


00:19:38.724 --> 00:19:42.592
Ravi, what frigging god did you pray to?


00:19:43.829 --> 00:19:47.925
Guy, yeah, it seems someone's
not being entirely honest here.


00:19:49.902 --> 00:19:52.097
Katie, somebody get that door!


00:19:53.239 --> 00:19:54.797
So...


00:19:55.675 --> 00:19:57.802
...that meeting today...


00:19:57.977 --> 00:20:00.775
...it was obvious
that your dad doesn't get you.


00:20:01.113 --> 00:20:03.172
He's an idiot for not liking your music.


00:20:03.349 --> 00:20:05.783
Well, it's... It's complicated.


00:20:06.052 --> 00:20:07.246
I'm gonna just, uh...


00:20:08.721 --> 00:20:10.621
Is it as complicated as me...


00:20:10.790 --> 00:20:13.918
...getting stuck outside
in only a welcome mat?


00:20:14.193 --> 00:20:17.924
That's not complicated.
That is a gift from God.


00:20:22.835 --> 00:20:25.633
Luke. Katie. What are you doing?


00:20:25.805 --> 00:20:28.865
Well, it seems your brother
is Satan's very own personal Mini-Me.


00:20:29.041 --> 00:20:31.305
Oh, I know, tell me about it. Come on in.


00:20:35.281 --> 00:20:36.942
Oh, my God, did you work out today?


00:20:38.617 --> 00:20:39.914
- Sit down.
- Ooh, look at this.


00:20:40.086 --> 00:20:43.180
- Ha, ha. Some lemonade.
- Why, thank you.


00:20:43.355 --> 00:20:45.823
You know, my stepsister,
she has body issues...


00:20:45.991 --> 00:20:48.152
...so I don't like
to discourage her nudity.


00:20:48.327 --> 00:20:49.521
That's interesting.


00:20:49.695 --> 00:20:52.459
- She's absolutely lovely...
- Would you like an appetizer?


00:20:52.631 --> 00:20:53.859
<i>Oh, fromage.</i>


00:20:54.033 --> 00:20:55.660
I only have cheese.


00:20:58.838 --> 00:21:00.806
I just got off the phone
with Guy Morgan.


00:21:00.973 --> 00:21:02.873
Your phone.


00:21:05.911 --> 00:21:08.778
He just loved that little demo
you left him.


00:21:08.948 --> 00:21:10.506
I have underestimated you.


00:21:11.083 --> 00:21:12.914
It'd make me proud
if I cared about you.


00:21:13.085 --> 00:21:16.179
- I didn't lie about anything.
- Oh, but, chicken, you did.


00:21:16.355 --> 00:21:18.983
At least that's what Guy thinks,
now that I've clarified.


00:21:19.158 --> 00:21:23.356
I told him it was Bev's demo
and that you stole it from her.


00:21:23.529 --> 00:21:26.794
- But you can't do that. That's my song.
- It's Bev's song.


00:21:26.966 --> 00:21:30.402
And Guy can't wait to see her perform it
at the Showcase.


00:21:30.569 --> 00:21:33.697
If you try to contact him, I'll deny
everything and lock you in the basement.


00:21:33.873 --> 00:21:39.004
- She can't sing to save her life.
- No, but you can, can't you?


00:21:40.279 --> 00:21:42.440
Now, let's hear this amazing voice.


00:21:47.853 --> 00:21:52.483
<i>Like a malignant tumor
She's got no sense of humor</i>


00:21:52.658 --> 00:21:56.754
<i>Just like a swollen blister
It's best to just resist her</i>


00:21:56.929 --> 00:22:00.695
<i>She's not exactly a witch
She's just a terrible bi...</i>


00:22:01.167 --> 00:22:02.828
Well, your lyrics stink.


00:22:03.002 --> 00:22:05.163
But Guy's right, you've got chops.


00:22:08.407 --> 00:22:11.103
Do you know what other instruments
I'm good at?


00:22:11.677 --> 00:22:15.135
I have a feeling I could get in trouble
with a question like that.


00:22:15.581 --> 00:22:17.549
I like trouble.


00:22:19.084 --> 00:22:20.210
Hey, kids.


00:22:21.520 --> 00:22:24.956
- Good evening, Miss Van Ravensway.
- Sorry, I need you to go. Now.


00:22:25.124 --> 00:22:27.888
Family emergency. I need Bev
to help me pass a kidney stone.


00:22:28.060 --> 00:22:31.894
- So she had a lovely evening. Ta-ta.
- Are you trying to ruin my life?


00:22:32.198 --> 00:22:37.431
I have figured out a way for you
to wow Guy Morgan in the Showcase.


00:22:37.636 --> 00:22:40.104
- So you do think I've improved?
- Oh, no, honey.


00:22:40.372 --> 00:22:42.932
But my month of spiritual devotion
has taught me...


00:22:43.108 --> 00:22:45.076
...that God works in annoying ways.


00:22:45.244 --> 00:22:48.304
How am I to wow Guy Morgan
if I supposedly can't sing?


00:22:48.480 --> 00:22:51.540
You can't, but Katie can.


00:22:51.717 --> 00:22:54.413
- What?
- I know. Like I said, annoying.


00:22:54.587 --> 00:22:57.886
We'll record her voice
and you will lip synch.


00:22:58.057 --> 00:22:59.888
What if I don't want to?


00:23:00.993 --> 00:23:04.724
Don't you get snarky with me,
you ungrateful toad.


00:23:04.897 --> 00:23:06.956
- I saved your life.
- You didn't do anything.


00:23:07.132 --> 00:23:09.396
- My dad married you.
- Yeah, and then he died.


00:23:09.568 --> 00:23:13.129
I tried to put you in foster care,
but they was all fulled up on ugly.


00:23:13.305 --> 00:23:14.795
- Funny.
- I thought it was...


00:23:14.974 --> 00:23:16.441
...because you don't wanna look bad.


00:23:18.043 --> 00:23:20.170
Katie, if you don't sing...


00:23:20.346 --> 00:23:23.474
...I'm gonna find a way for that savings
your dad left to disappear.


00:23:23.883 --> 00:23:28.081
That means, you forget college,
moving out, you're stuck here with me.


00:23:28.254 --> 00:23:32.088
But, pumpkin, we're gonna have
so much fun growing old together.


00:23:32.258 --> 00:23:35.159
Why don't you just have her perform
if you like her so much?


00:23:35.327 --> 00:23:37.591
Because, honey, look at you.


00:23:37.763 --> 00:23:39.890
You are a star.


00:23:40.065 --> 00:23:44.263
That is what Guy Morgan needs.
You, the star.


00:23:44.436 --> 00:23:45.994
I'm a star.


00:23:46.171 --> 00:23:50.335
- A bright, gassy star.
- Yes, you are.


00:23:50.509 --> 00:23:52.909
And Guy Morgan is gonna
give you a swimming pool...


00:23:53.078 --> 00:23:55.046
...shaped just like Colin Farrell.


00:23:55.214 --> 00:23:56.772
Every part of him.


00:23:56.949 --> 00:24:00.476
Or, Bev, you could just see every part
of Colin Farrell on the Internet.


00:24:00.653 --> 00:24:03.417
And just leave me out of this.


00:24:04.690 --> 00:24:07.250
- Okay, so how do we do this?
- First rule of Lie Club...


00:24:07.426 --> 00:24:09.326
...is don't talk about Lie Club.


00:24:09.929 --> 00:24:11.829
Which includes you, Katie.


00:24:11.997 --> 00:24:14.693
As far as everyone knows,
you can't sing.


00:24:14.867 --> 00:24:16.926
And no more talking to Luke or Guy.


00:24:17.102 --> 00:24:18.467
Are we clear?


00:24:18.904 --> 00:24:20.098
Crystal.


00:24:22.041 --> 00:24:25.033
Yeah, Dad, we're about to meet
some fresh talent right now.


00:24:25.210 --> 00:24:29.203
Remember when you signed Jay-Z?
No, you passed on him, my bad.


00:24:29.381 --> 00:24:31.849
Um, this is like that,
except it's gonna be brilliant.


00:24:32.017 --> 00:24:33.348
Yeah. Okay.


00:24:33.519 --> 00:24:35.646
- Yeah, okay. Bye.
- Dude, what'd he say?


00:24:35.821 --> 00:24:37.345
These guys you told me about are good?


00:24:37.523 --> 00:24:40.890
Yes. The Oral Majority has potential.
They'll be here any second.


00:24:41.060 --> 00:24:43.756
Talking about potential,
how was your little date with Bev?


00:24:43.929 --> 00:24:46.193
- Her mom kicked me out.
- I told you. Bev is drama.


00:24:46.365 --> 00:24:47.923
Technically, it was Gail's drama.


00:24:48.100 --> 00:24:50.227
But Bev's interesting, man. She's...


00:24:50.402 --> 00:24:51.869
I'm worried she's bonkers.


00:24:52.037 --> 00:24:54.870
See, my last girlfriend, she was hot,
but absolutely mental.


00:24:55.040 --> 00:24:57.702
I need a girl who's not gonna be
shipped to the loony bin.


00:24:57.876 --> 00:24:59.639
Hang on, I'm gonna hit the facilities.


00:24:59.812 --> 00:25:01.507
Facilities. That's a new one.


00:25:01.947 --> 00:25:04.643
- Hey, man. Sorry we're late.
- Hey, what's good, y'all?


00:25:04.817 --> 00:25:07.547
Nobody talks to my boy
until he comes from the facilities.


00:25:07.720 --> 00:25:08.914
We're here to impress.


00:25:09.088 --> 00:25:11.352
- Clear, right?
- Got it.


00:25:15.194 --> 00:25:17.662
<i>When you're fighting just to keep it sane</i>


00:25:17.830 --> 00:25:20.094
<i>Throw your will
At the eye of the hurricane</i>


00:25:20.265 --> 00:25:22.460
<i>- Sing it out
- Eh-oh, eh-oh, eh-oh</i>


00:25:22.634 --> 00:25:26.001
<i>- Help me sing it out
- Eh-oh, eh-oh, eh-oh</i>


00:25:26.171 --> 00:25:28.696
<i>If you wanna find out who you are
Stop running</i>


00:25:28.874 --> 00:25:32.139
<i>In the end you'll figure out
It's all about nothing</i>


00:25:32.311 --> 00:25:37.613
<i>All night, it's gonna be all right
Hey, hey, hey, hey</i>


00:25:37.783 --> 00:25:44.518
<i>All right
Turn your dreams into your life</i>


00:25:45.724 --> 00:25:47.214
That's good.


00:25:54.266 --> 00:25:57.565
I'm clean. No one followed me.
And I got your intel.


00:25:58.404 --> 00:26:00.736
Oh, Katie, baby, your life sucks.


00:26:00.906 --> 00:26:02.806
Trust me, it gets worse.


00:26:03.842 --> 00:26:07.437
Okay, dude, those guys, they
just went Oral Majority on me in there...


00:26:07.613 --> 00:26:09.808
- I was trying to hold them back...
- You're right.


00:26:09.982 --> 00:26:11.916
They have potential and they're great.


00:26:12.084 --> 00:26:17.317
But first, my talent-finding friend,
promise me no more auditions in the bogs.


00:26:17.489 --> 00:26:19.684
- The what?
- The loo.


00:26:20.225 --> 00:26:21.988
- Bathroom. Toilet.
- Got it.


00:26:22.161 --> 00:26:24.755
All right. Okay, come on.
I wanna show you something.


00:26:25.364 --> 00:26:28.663
So now I have to rehearse in secret.


00:26:28.834 --> 00:26:30.301
Why not not rehearse?


00:26:30.469 --> 00:26:32.494
Make Bev sound bad. What do you care?


00:26:32.671 --> 00:26:35.663
No song, no savings account. No life.


00:26:37.843 --> 00:26:40.277
People. Coming. Now.


00:26:43.816 --> 00:26:45.647
Okay.


00:26:46.218 --> 00:26:48.584
Dude, what are we doing?
The suspense is killing me.


00:26:48.921 --> 00:26:50.684
Can you grab the mike?


00:26:50.856 --> 00:26:52.847
Not about to serenade
a brother, are you?


00:26:53.025 --> 00:26:54.856
Dude, with bromance, comes a fine line.


00:26:55.027 --> 00:26:57.325
That I shall not cross.


00:26:57.796 --> 00:27:00.094
So sing something.


00:27:01.767 --> 00:27:03.234
Okay.


00:27:07.372 --> 00:27:10.170
<i>I'm lost in a world
That rattles my brain</i>


00:27:10.342 --> 00:27:12.833
<i>I'm cleaning up my life
From the mess you made</i>


00:27:13.011 --> 00:27:14.410
<i>Oh, oh</i>


00:27:14.880 --> 00:27:16.871
<i>Whoa, oh, oh, oh</i>


00:27:18.684 --> 00:27:21.152
<i>My soul's in debt, but my bills are paid</i>


00:27:21.320 --> 00:27:23.845
<i>I'd give anything just to make an escape</i>


00:27:24.022 --> 00:27:25.614
<i>Oh, oh</i>


00:27:26.125 --> 00:27:27.752
<i>Whoa, oh, oh, oh</i>


00:27:28.760 --> 00:27:31.695
<i>So you can keep
Knocking, knocking, knocking</i>


00:27:31.864 --> 00:27:34.196
<i>Baby, you're rockin'
But there ain't no way I'm ever letting you in</i>


00:27:34.366 --> 00:27:35.833
<i>He's amazing.</i>


00:27:37.236 --> 00:27:38.897
<i>Not again</i>


00:27:39.838 --> 00:27:42.671
<i>So keep on
Knocking, knocking, knocking</i>


00:27:42.841 --> 00:27:48.040
<i>But, baby, you're better off walking
'Cause I ain't gonna let you in</i>


00:27:48.213 --> 00:27:49.771
<i>Never again</i>


00:27:50.883 --> 00:27:53.477
<i>I went out on a limb again</i>


00:27:53.652 --> 00:27:56.212
<i>I guess I had to lose to win</i>


00:27:56.388 --> 00:28:00.757
<i>I was too confused to know
Which way to turn</i>


00:28:02.161 --> 00:28:04.823
<i>- And she could be a millionaire...
- Crap.</i>


00:28:04.997 --> 00:28:07.261
<i>- Gail needs me to drive her home.
- I don't care</i>


00:28:07.432 --> 00:28:10.094
<i>'Cause, baby, there's nobody home</i>


00:28:10.269 --> 00:28:12.760
<i>Nobody's home at all, yeah</i>


00:28:17.242 --> 00:28:19.369
- What? Did you write that?
- Yeah.


00:28:19.545 --> 00:28:22.173
Reminds me of, um... Uh...


00:28:22.347 --> 00:28:25.680
- Danger Fruit, right? Danger Fruit.
- Ha, ha. Because I wrote their album too.


00:28:25.951 --> 00:28:28.442
Shut up. Took me forever
to find that bootleg online.


00:28:28.620 --> 00:28:30.611
- I love that album. That's crazy.
- Yeah.


00:28:30.789 --> 00:28:33.087
My dad doesn't know.
And he thought the record...


00:28:33.258 --> 00:28:34.953
...was a pile of crap.


00:28:35.227 --> 00:28:36.922
He thinks writing's a waste of time.


00:28:37.362 --> 00:28:41.196
Because he basically wants me
to be like him. Only with better hair.


00:28:41.667 --> 00:28:45.763
But the first thing I thought when
I heard those guys in the urinals was...


00:28:45.938 --> 00:28:46.962
...good acoustics.


00:28:47.372 --> 00:28:51.206
Second thought was these guys,
these guys could be great.


00:28:51.376 --> 00:28:52.968
If you gave them your song.


00:28:54.379 --> 00:28:56.040
Mate, that's a brilliant idea.


00:28:56.782 --> 00:28:59.478
- So put them in the Showcase?
- Put them in the Showcase.


00:28:59.651 --> 00:29:00.982
Yeah.


00:29:02.654 --> 00:29:09.184
<i>You can never tell where this might go</i>


00:29:09.494 --> 00:29:10.791
You wrote that song today?


00:29:10.963 --> 00:29:14.421
- You've been home for what, two hours?
- It's like an answer to his song.


00:29:14.700 --> 00:29:15.997
You really like this guy.


00:29:16.168 --> 00:29:17.863
Yeah, I'm an idiot.


00:29:18.036 --> 00:29:20.231
You have to sing that for him.


00:29:20.405 --> 00:29:23.897
What if you sang to him in secret?


00:29:25.711 --> 00:29:28.509
At the dance. Ta-da.


00:29:32.117 --> 00:29:34.950
Okay, I know the card's
like, really cheesy, but...


00:29:36.989 --> 00:29:39.457
Oh, God, I hope you like it.


00:29:39.791 --> 00:29:43.283
Ange, it's beautiful,
but are you crazy?


00:29:43.462 --> 00:29:45.487
No, I know you're crazy.


00:29:45.664 --> 00:29:46.688
Am not.


00:29:47.733 --> 00:29:50.725
- What if he doesn't even like me?
- You'll both be in disguise.


00:29:50.902 --> 00:29:53.598
It's your chance to see
if he was really flirting with you.


00:29:53.772 --> 00:29:56.332
I was naked. Of course he was flirting.


00:29:56.508 --> 00:29:59.204
And why even torture myself?
It's not like I can have him.


00:29:59.378 --> 00:30:01.312
Why not? Tell him how you feel.


00:30:01.480 --> 00:30:05.507
If he feels the same way, you can reveal
your hot self and he won't tell Gail.


00:30:05.884 --> 00:30:08.978
And if he hates the song,
leave the disguise on.


00:30:11.923 --> 00:30:13.447
Okay.


00:30:13.759 --> 00:30:15.351
I'm going to the dance.


00:30:15.527 --> 00:30:16.858
That's my girl.


00:30:17.129 --> 00:30:21.122
<i>Maurice, no, no.
Again, in Français, longer legs.</i>


00:30:21.300 --> 00:30:24.599
I wouldn't go in your closet
for a little while if I were you.


00:30:24.770 --> 00:30:26.533
What? Why?


00:30:26.705 --> 00:30:28.070
Hey. Wake up.


00:30:31.977 --> 00:30:33.535
Katie!


00:30:33.712 --> 00:30:37.148
The cat has pooped in my closet.
I need you to clean it up.


00:30:37.316 --> 00:30:38.806
Go.


00:30:38.984 --> 00:30:40.713
I told you we don't have a cat.


00:30:40.886 --> 00:30:42.217
Angie, heads up.


00:30:44.189 --> 00:30:45.486
Katie!


00:30:50.696 --> 00:30:52.425
What's going on?


00:30:52.597 --> 00:30:54.030
Nothing.


00:30:54.199 --> 00:30:57.327
I am, uh, re-organizing and labeling. I...


00:30:57.502 --> 00:30:59.800
I took up crochet.
Do you want new socks?


00:30:59.971 --> 00:31:04.032
I would make you a sweater, but I hear
that the arms, that they're really hard.


00:31:07.279 --> 00:31:11.443
Oh, you thought you could sneak off
and go to the dance.


00:31:11.616 --> 00:31:13.846
After what you pulled today with Guy.


00:31:14.019 --> 00:31:15.452
Oh, no, no.


00:31:15.620 --> 00:31:18.111
Oh, no, no, no.


00:31:18.290 --> 00:31:20.588
You're on Victor watch tonight...


00:31:20.759 --> 00:31:23.455
...tomorrow night and every night.


00:31:23.628 --> 00:31:24.652
Fun.


00:31:24.830 --> 00:31:27.958
I'll give Victor all the mothering
you don't have time for.


00:31:28.133 --> 00:31:31.534
Oh, I wish you could be my mommy.


00:31:32.404 --> 00:31:34.429
I'm off to my cinnamon colonic.


00:31:38.410 --> 00:31:40.776
Hey. Get down.
You're gonna break yourself.


00:31:41.113 --> 00:31:43.377
Or worse, the furniture.


00:31:43.682 --> 00:31:46.776
Hello?
- Hey.


00:31:47.052 --> 00:31:50.215
- You look like you're having fun.
- Always.


00:31:50.555 --> 00:31:53.615
Well, I couldn't let you not go to the dance
without me.


00:31:53.792 --> 00:31:56.192
Besides, we have six hours
of shirtless Team Jacob.


00:31:56.361 --> 00:31:59.296
So let's just get this party started.


00:31:59.464 --> 00:32:03.491
- So is Victor driving you nuts?
- I swear to you, he's not human.


00:32:03.769 --> 00:32:07.068
I mean, can you really blame him, though?
Just look at this family.


00:32:08.273 --> 00:32:09.570
Victor, what are you doing?


00:32:19.551 --> 00:32:21.815
Oh, no. Great.


00:32:21.987 --> 00:32:24.182
Eh, she actually looks prettier
that way.


00:32:24.790 --> 00:32:27.816
True. Ugh. Whatever.


00:32:28.994 --> 00:32:32.122
Why did I ever think that tonight
could've been something special.


00:32:32.898 --> 00:32:35.162
Think Bev's all over Luke at the dance
right now?


00:32:35.333 --> 00:32:37.631
They're probably making out. See?


00:32:37.803 --> 00:32:41.000
- Victor, give it a rest.
- Just check it out. Come on.


00:32:44.209 --> 00:32:46.837
<i>Luke is gonna produce
whoever wins the Showcase.</i>


00:32:47.012 --> 00:32:50.072
<i>So we need a little insurance.</i>


00:32:50.248 --> 00:32:53.445
<i>- I know what I'm doing, Mother.
Do you?</i>


00:32:54.352 --> 00:32:57.219
I can't take it anymore, okay?


00:32:57.389 --> 00:32:59.448
I'm taking my life into my own hands.


00:32:59.624 --> 00:33:00.716
I'm talking to Luke.


00:33:01.326 --> 00:33:03.817
- Finally.
- Okay, but we have gotta be home...


00:33:03.995 --> 00:33:05.462
...before Gail gets here.


00:33:06.198 --> 00:33:07.529
What about the demon spawn?


00:33:07.699 --> 00:33:08.723
Mm-hm.


00:33:08.900 --> 00:33:10.299
Right.


00:33:11.303 --> 00:33:12.702
Okay, just watch him.


00:33:15.774 --> 00:33:17.036
Hmm.


00:33:21.847 --> 00:33:23.838
Is that all you've got, Angela?


00:33:24.516 --> 00:33:25.540
Ravi?


00:33:27.219 --> 00:33:29.744
My sister could catch that, jerknut.


00:33:29.921 --> 00:33:32.355
Put some nuts in that sack, ref.


00:33:34.493 --> 00:33:37.053
Miss Katie, I am most startled.


00:33:37.229 --> 00:33:38.423
Obviously.


00:33:38.964 --> 00:33:41.455
All right. All right. Don't hate me.


00:33:41.633 --> 00:33:43.191
Okay, don't hate me. I'm sorry.


00:33:43.368 --> 00:33:46.735
But my name ain't Ravi. It's Tony.


00:33:47.272 --> 00:33:50.400
- Tony.
- Tony Gupta from Jersey.


00:33:50.575 --> 00:33:53.237
- From Jersey.
- I am half Indian.


00:33:53.612 --> 00:33:57.013
My friends call me Meatball
because I'm half Italian.


00:33:57.182 --> 00:33:59.047
Truth is I always wanted to be an actor.


00:33:59.417 --> 00:34:00.941
But I never got my shot.


00:34:01.119 --> 00:34:03.349
I'm working at KFC,
and one day, Gail comes in...


00:34:03.522 --> 00:34:05.922
...she's like, "Are you Indian?"
I'm like, "What?"


00:34:06.091 --> 00:34:08.286
She's like, "Are you a guru?"
I'm like:


00:34:08.460 --> 00:34:09.950
"Who is asking?"


00:34:10.228 --> 00:34:13.595
She says, "Someone
who's paying for some spiritual guidance."


00:34:13.765 --> 00:34:16.359
And I'm like, "Whaa! It's a miracle!"


00:34:16.535 --> 00:34:20.904
I finally get a chance to do
a total immersion into a character.


00:34:21.206 --> 00:34:23.470
Real training and I get paid.
Are you kidding me?


00:34:23.642 --> 00:34:26.042
Ravi is my King Lear.


00:34:26.378 --> 00:34:29.006
<i>You wanna hear
the monologue from My Fair Lady?</i>


00:34:29.180 --> 00:34:30.374
- Oy, mate.
- No, thanks.


00:34:31.583 --> 00:34:34.279
I'm sorry I barged in. Whoops.


00:34:37.088 --> 00:34:40.751
Your secret's safe with me, okay?
But I need to ask you a favor.


00:34:41.426 --> 00:34:43.485
- Meatball.
- Ha, Meatball.


00:34:43.662 --> 00:34:46.130
Please watch Victor tonight
so I can go to the dance?


00:34:46.298 --> 00:34:47.356
Are you kidding me? Done.


00:34:48.934 --> 00:34:50.265
Blow it up.


00:34:52.203 --> 00:34:53.761
Thank you.


00:35:03.582 --> 00:35:04.981
Whoa.


00:35:05.150 --> 00:35:07.778
How am I supposed to find Luke
if everybody's got a mask?


00:35:07.953 --> 00:35:11.013
I never said this was
gonna be easy. Let's do some recon.


00:35:12.390 --> 00:35:14.722
I am Assistant Principal
Dorothy Plumberg.


00:35:14.893 --> 00:35:18.124
No drinking. No texting. No kissing.


00:35:20.832 --> 00:35:23.801
Luke? No. Luke Morgan?


00:35:23.969 --> 00:35:27.598
No leaving the premises
and no experiencing joy of any kind.


00:35:28.306 --> 00:35:30.638
Luke? Ugh.


00:35:36.014 --> 00:35:37.447
Where is he?


00:35:38.283 --> 00:35:41.081
That reminds me.
I got a new act for you to listen to.


00:35:41.252 --> 00:35:42.913
- Now?
- No time like it.


00:35:43.088 --> 00:35:45.522
- Dude, not again...
- We're called Big Pain Ticket.


00:35:49.027 --> 00:35:52.588
<i>I wanna kiss your apocalypse</i>


00:35:52.764 --> 00:35:56.097
<i>Wrap you in my Armageddon</i>


00:35:56.267 --> 00:35:58.462
<i>Sing you a twisted serenade</i>


00:35:58.670 --> 00:36:01.400
They're good, but I'm worried
that chain saw's unsafe.


00:36:01.573 --> 00:36:04.007
Dude, the chain saw's,
like, the best part.


00:36:10.815 --> 00:36:11.873
I think I found him.


00:36:12.050 --> 00:36:14.314
Well, he is blond.


00:36:17.422 --> 00:36:19.720
Oh, my God, what is she doing here?


00:36:21.626 --> 00:36:23.924
I hate teenage desperation.


00:36:24.095 --> 00:36:25.494
What are you doing here?


00:36:25.664 --> 00:36:28.497
Oh, honey, the prize pig
doesn't win the blue ribbon...


00:36:28.667 --> 00:36:30.692
...by covering up its third best asset.


00:36:30.869 --> 00:36:33.804
A, what does that even mean
and, B, did you just call me a pig?


00:36:33.972 --> 00:36:35.803
Honey, I saw you making sweet love...


00:36:35.974 --> 00:36:38.442
...to a plate of Swedish meatballs
at the snack table.


00:36:40.879 --> 00:36:43.006
It's now or never, babe.


00:36:44.549 --> 00:36:47.985
- What if she recognizes me?
- I'll distract her. Go.


00:36:48.153 --> 00:36:50.348
- So was I right or was I right?
- You were right.


00:36:50.522 --> 00:36:53.389
You have very cool taste.
Any more auditions in the men's...


00:36:53.558 --> 00:36:55.492
...and you're fired.


00:36:58.530 --> 00:37:02.057
- I know your secret.
- Which secret is that?


00:37:04.669 --> 00:37:06.159
I heard you sing at school.


00:37:06.404 --> 00:37:07.530
You were amazing.


00:37:07.706 --> 00:37:08.764
Do I know you?


00:37:13.111 --> 00:37:15.705
- I wanna show you something.
- What's your name?


00:37:18.049 --> 00:37:20.108
Angela, what are you doing?


00:37:20.752 --> 00:37:23.243
I'd like to make a request.


00:37:27.759 --> 00:37:30.592
I will make your night. I promise.


00:37:30.762 --> 00:37:32.127
Miss Van R.


00:37:32.764 --> 00:37:35.164
Is it true you wanted to be a dancer
when you were younger...


00:37:35.333 --> 00:37:36.527
...but were never good enough?


00:37:37.902 --> 00:37:39.563
Who told you that?


00:37:57.288 --> 00:37:58.721
Well, now, how lovely.


00:37:58.890 --> 00:38:02.087
But I've seen better dancing
in a Filipino prison, sugar.


00:38:02.260 --> 00:38:03.386
Oh!


00:38:03.561 --> 00:38:07.793
Really? Because I think
I just challenged you to a dance battle.


00:38:12.137 --> 00:38:15.231
Would Luke Morgan please pick up
the white courtesy phone?


00:38:15.406 --> 00:38:18.307
Luke Morgan, white courtesy phone.


00:38:23.081 --> 00:38:25.811
Hold on. What is that?
You've never seen a guitar before?


00:38:26.151 --> 00:38:28.847
You hid a guitar in there.
You hiding anything else?


00:38:29.020 --> 00:38:30.282
Follow me.


00:38:35.326 --> 00:38:37.157
Oh, wow.


00:38:39.631 --> 00:38:45.194
Madam, while your exquisite eyes
tell of a radiant, but mischievous beauty...


00:38:46.070 --> 00:38:47.970
...I have grown impatient.


00:38:48.139 --> 00:38:51.836
Off with your veil,
so that I may know the truth.


00:38:53.344 --> 00:38:54.538
Or not.


00:38:56.815 --> 00:38:59.841
I'm hoping this answers
a lot of your questions.


00:39:06.057 --> 00:39:09.618
<i>I can see it from the spark in your eyes</i>


00:39:10.929 --> 00:39:15.161
<i>You believe in all the things
You've denied</i>


00:39:15.333 --> 00:39:18.860
<i>You wanna fly
And leave your worries behind</i>


00:39:19.037 --> 00:39:23.030
<i>Don't you? Don't you?</i>


00:39:25.009 --> 00:39:28.342
<i>Well, now I'm knocking
At your front door</i>


00:39:30.114 --> 00:39:33.811
<i>And I'm looking for the right cure</i>


00:39:34.485 --> 00:39:38.182
<i>I'm still a little bit unsure</i>


00:39:38.656 --> 00:39:41.489
Okay, now take off that veil.


00:39:41.960 --> 00:39:43.052
Uh-uh.


00:42:21.986 --> 00:42:24.580
I think I've blown something.


00:42:24.756 --> 00:42:27.816
Does anyone else smell cinnamon?


00:42:30.428 --> 00:42:31.986
Move it, fatso.


00:42:33.731 --> 00:42:40.330
<i>You can never tell where this might go</i>


00:42:41.072 --> 00:42:44.701
Okay, you are blowing my mind.
You have to show me who you are.


00:42:57.255 --> 00:42:58.688
- We have to go.
- What?


00:42:58.856 --> 00:43:00.881
- Come.
- No, Ange.


00:43:01.059 --> 00:43:03.619
In the middle of a really big moment
right now.


00:43:03.795 --> 00:43:05.763
Someone had an accident
and went home.


00:43:08.232 --> 00:43:09.597
I'm so sorry.


00:43:10.301 --> 00:43:11.529
What...? You...?


00:43:12.236 --> 00:43:13.897
Hey. Wait.


00:43:14.072 --> 00:43:15.300
But who are you?


00:43:15.473 --> 00:43:18.067
Over here. Go, go, go.


00:43:26.217 --> 00:43:29.243
- We beat her.
- I love you for this.


00:43:47.705 --> 00:43:49.730
Interesting babysitting attire.


00:43:50.508 --> 00:43:53.443
I should've known
you'd go behind my back again.


00:43:53.878 --> 00:43:56.813
And that Paula Abdul wannabe,
trying to distract me.


00:43:57.148 --> 00:43:59.343
Don't talk about her like that.


00:44:01.352 --> 00:44:04.515
Your friend wants to be a choreographer,
if memory serves.


00:44:04.689 --> 00:44:08.250
She might've made a decent one
if she hadn't gotten herself expelled.


00:44:08.426 --> 00:44:10.690
Guess she can kiss
them Juilliard dreams goodbye.


00:44:10.862 --> 00:44:13.922
Look, I'll do whatever you want.
Okay? Just leave Ange out of this.


00:44:14.232 --> 00:44:17.360
That depends if you pull another stunt
like tonight, sugar.


00:44:18.269 --> 00:44:21.397
- I won't.
- I'll be taking this.


00:44:27.912 --> 00:44:31.143
Only her eyes were piercing out
through this veil, but her voice...


00:44:31.315 --> 00:44:33.374
How hot was the girl
on a scale of one to 10?


00:44:33.551 --> 00:44:35.485
- An 11.
- The hotness scale only goes 10.


00:44:35.653 --> 00:44:37.348
Yeah, this girl has love potential.


00:44:37.522 --> 00:44:39.820
- Ooh, love.
- Shut it.


00:44:41.192 --> 00:44:45.322
We are gonna do this for hours
until we get it right. Even if it takes hours.


00:44:46.297 --> 00:44:49.892
Now, sing like your life depends on it.
Because, sugar, it does.


00:44:50.968 --> 00:44:52.595
We're recording.


00:44:52.904 --> 00:44:54.735
<i>Plug in the mike</i>


00:44:54.906 --> 00:44:56.134
<i>Open the curtain</i>


00:44:56.741 --> 00:44:58.675
<i>Turn on the lights</i>


00:44:58.843 --> 00:45:00.572
<i>I'm through rehearsing</i>


00:45:00.745 --> 00:45:03.077
- Dang, she's good, man.
- Told you, man.


00:45:03.247 --> 00:45:04.475
Check this out, all right?


00:45:04.649 --> 00:45:08.244
Thirty-nine girls in the singing program
which means 85 percent...


00:45:08.419 --> 00:45:10.250
...have music during the sixth period.


00:45:10.421 --> 00:45:12.252
So your girl's in one of those rooms.


00:45:12.456 --> 00:45:14.481
<i>The feeling ignites</i>


00:45:14.659 --> 00:45:15.819
<i>I'm in control</i>


00:45:15.993 --> 00:45:17.961
Oh, cut. Cut.


00:45:18.129 --> 00:45:19.994
That was subpar at best.


00:45:20.164 --> 00:45:22.689
From the top, pretty please.


00:45:23.434 --> 00:45:26.733
<i>Amazing grace</i>


00:45:26.904 --> 00:45:28.462
It's cool, I got this.


00:45:28.639 --> 00:45:31.005
Ladies, all my single ladies.


00:45:31.175 --> 00:45:34.201
My boy Luke here has a special favor
to ask of you, all right?


00:45:34.378 --> 00:45:37.472
He needs vocals
for this big show coming up, so...


00:45:37.648 --> 00:45:39.206
- My name is...
- Luke Morgan.


00:45:39.650 --> 00:45:42.517
You will put me in the Showcase.
Oh, yes, you will.


00:45:43.054 --> 00:45:46.615
- Maybe I could ask you to sing first?
- I am so gonna rock your world.


00:45:46.891 --> 00:45:50.224
<i>I love the way you love me, Luke</i>


00:45:50.394 --> 00:45:52.988
<i>Inside my head every night</i>


00:45:53.164 --> 00:45:55.632
<i>You come and kiss me good night</i>


00:45:55.800 --> 00:45:58.894
<i>Whatever you see is what you get</i>


00:45:59.070 --> 00:46:01.595
Why don't you not suck
and do it again, okay?


00:46:03.341 --> 00:46:07.937
<i>I wanna be with you forever...</i>


00:46:08.112 --> 00:46:11.081
What is going on in here? Disgusting.


00:46:11.249 --> 00:46:14.082
You two boys are not in my class.
Stop. Wait.


00:46:20.124 --> 00:46:23.321
Stop. Wait. Stop.


00:46:42.446 --> 00:46:44.744
<i>I got nothing to lose</i>


00:46:44.915 --> 00:46:46.109
<i>I've been exposed</i>


00:46:46.284 --> 00:46:48.582
<i>I'm paying my dues</i>


00:46:48.753 --> 00:46:50.118
<i>Playing the role</i>


00:46:50.955 --> 00:46:53.082
- Oh, really?
- We are back where we started.


00:46:53.257 --> 00:46:54.383
This is not good.


00:46:55.960 --> 00:46:57.757
That's her. That's her voice.


00:46:57.928 --> 00:46:59.759
Don't think you can get away from me.


00:46:59.930 --> 00:47:02.330
- Step aside. Step aside.
- Please. Wait.


00:47:02.500 --> 00:47:05.936
Okay. But first, why don't you
just both audition for me.


00:47:06.103 --> 00:47:07.127
Listen...


00:47:07.305 --> 00:47:10.741
<i>Luke, you are the one for me, yes you are</i>


00:47:10.908 --> 00:47:12.569
<i>You just don't know it yet</i>


00:47:24.422 --> 00:47:28.415
<i>Make you believe in me</i>


00:47:28.592 --> 00:47:31.584
<i>I can be what you want me to be</i>


00:47:31.762 --> 00:47:35.391
<i>Tonight is the night
Where I make you see</i>


00:47:35.566 --> 00:47:39.502
<i>That I can be
Anything, anything, anything</i>


00:47:39.670 --> 00:47:43.470
<i>I'll make you believe in me</i>


00:47:44.008 --> 00:47:46.909
<i>I can be what you want me to be</i>


00:47:47.078 --> 00:47:50.138
<i>Tonight is the night
Where I make you see</i>


00:47:51.949 --> 00:47:53.883
It was you?


00:47:54.552 --> 00:47:57.646
- Oh, sorry to interrupt.
- Oh, no, honey. Interrupt away.


00:47:58.589 --> 00:48:02.423
I didn't think I'd see you. It was killing me.
Because I felt like we connected.


00:48:04.061 --> 00:48:07.087
Excuse me.
Uh, how exactly did you two connect?


00:48:07.264 --> 00:48:10.028
Yeah, how did we? I mean, we did.


00:48:10.201 --> 00:48:12.328
- Through...
- With your lyrics. They just...


00:48:12.970 --> 00:48:15.700
- I can't get them out of my head.
- My lyrics. Yeah.


00:48:15.973 --> 00:48:17.736
Well, how wonderful.


00:48:17.908 --> 00:48:21.275
But, uh, Bev has to prepare
for her Showcase audition.


00:48:21.445 --> 00:48:23.709
Oh, no. She doesn't need to audition.
You're in.


00:48:25.216 --> 00:48:27.013
Do you wanna grab a bite later?


00:48:27.184 --> 00:48:28.276
- Yeah.
Wait.


00:48:29.220 --> 00:48:30.687
You have a date with detention.


00:48:30.855 --> 00:48:32.322
Actually, he has a date with me.


00:48:32.490 --> 00:48:34.219
Dear me, did I not fire you?


00:48:34.392 --> 00:48:37.088
- I have tenure.
- One call and you're wearing a paper hat...


00:48:37.261 --> 00:48:40.389
...that says "Welcome to McDonald's.
How may I take your order?"


00:48:40.564 --> 00:48:42.054
- Five calls.
- Two calls and text.


00:48:42.233 --> 00:48:44.133
Two calls, a text, several long e-mails.


00:48:44.301 --> 00:48:47.099
One text and a Tweet.
- One text and a re-Tweet.


00:48:47.271 --> 00:48:49.637
Oh, for God's sakes,
go lick a chalkboard.


00:48:49.807 --> 00:48:51.274
Fine.


00:48:52.076 --> 00:48:53.600
I hate you.


00:48:57.248 --> 00:49:01.378
Okay. Um, I'd love to write a song with you.
Let's talk about it tonight?


00:49:01.652 --> 00:49:03.586
- I'd love to.
- Okay, you're on.


00:49:10.161 --> 00:49:11.788
I've always wanted to write a song.


00:49:11.962 --> 00:49:15.159
Maybe I'll write about my skin.
They say love tightens your pores.


00:49:15.332 --> 00:49:16.799
What rhymes with pores?


00:49:16.967 --> 00:49:19.765
Chores. Bores. Sores.


00:49:19.937 --> 00:49:22.132
Katie, I've got a new task for you.


